  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening youth electoral participation in Armenia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to increase youth participation in Armenia&#xfffd;s democratic processes by educating first-time voters (aged 16-18) and training young people (aged 18-25) as election observers ahead of the 2026 parliamentary elections. Through interactive voter education workshops, election observation training, and youth-led outreach campaigns, the project will empower 250 young Armenians to actively engage in the electoral process. The partnership combines Armenian and Danish youth expertise, promoting cross-national cooperation and fostering a new generation of informed, active, and responsible young voters and civic monitors.</narrative>
  </description>
